\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Original Investigations\'a0
\f1\b0 should be the student(s)\'92 original work. This can be accomplished with or without a mentor\'92s help. It should contain experimental data, or collected information, and should report novel results.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Review Articles\'a0
\f1\b0 provide a detailed critical review of a specific area of study based on the existing literature, including a meaningful synthesis.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Viewpoint Articles
\f1\b0 \'a0may address any important or controversial issues (i.e., \'93hot topics\'94) within any of the STEM fields. They should be focused, well informed, and provide a clear sense of direction.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
