\f0\b\fs42 \cf2 \cb3 Section Requirements\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa225\partightenfactor0

\fs30 \cf2 Title Page\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs28 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The title page must include a concise, descriptive title, and should include the name of each author and their institutional affiliation(s). The title page should clearly identify who the corresponding author is and list their contact information (address, email address, and telephone number). The title page should also contain the word count (excluding figures, tables, references, abstract, and title page).\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The title page template can be accessed and downloaded\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dlR9DNDj33RKmd5pDQ6_RmBT4lER8uhI/edit"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \ul \ulc6 \strokec6 here}}.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa225\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 Keywords\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs28 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Select three to five keywords with care, which will be used to help readers discover your paper. When determining appropriate keywords, put yourself in the position of someone who is trying to search for a paper like yours: What search terms would\'a0
\f2\i you
\f1\i0 \'a0use? Try to include these words in the text of the abstract and in the title of the paper.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa225\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 Abstract\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs28 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The abstract is the most important part of your paper since many readers will scan an abstract first before deciding to invest effort in reading the full article. An abstract should be no more than 250 words in length and act as a clear summary of the paper. It should clearly state the aim and scope of the research, the methods, results, conclusions, and implications of findings. The abstract should be broadly accessible (i.e., able to be understood by as many people as possible) and communicate the importance of the work being done. Abstracts should appear on the second page of the manuscript, not the title page.\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Guidelines and examples of abstracts are provided in the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1eY4gMekE2pnb3zOpTibtjJkte7on7HnT/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=105197192943580737038&rtpof=true&sd=true"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \ul \ulc6 \strokec6 Abstract Guidelines document}}.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa225\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 Introduction\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs28 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The introduction must provide context and background information for the appropriate academic audience.\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For original investigations\ulnone : state the focused research question(s), define the variables being studied, and make clear the objective, importance, and relevance of the work.\cb1 \
\ls5\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For review articles\ulnone : state the topic you are reviewing, why it is important, and why there is a need to compile and review information about that topic.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa225\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 Methods\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs28 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Materials and methods should be reported in a way that they can be reproduced by other investigators. It should explain the methods used and the reasons for using them. Provide sources for materials used whenever possible.\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl1\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For original investigations:\ulnone \'a0Your methods should be written as a step-by-step process and explain how variables were measured. It should also state and explain the choices of calculations and statistical analysis techniques.\cb1 \
\ls6\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For review articles:\ulnone \'a0Describe what databases you searched (i.e., MEDLINE, Embase, Google Scholar, etc.), what your inclusion and exclusion criteria were, and any statistical analyses performed. Additional search details, including a detailed search strategy, may be included in the appendix. For an example of a strong review article, see\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://journal.stemfellowship.org/doi/pdf/10.17975/sfj-2021-001"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \ul \ulc6 \strokec6 here}}.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa225\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 Results\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs28 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 In all results sections, it is important that you do not fabricate or plagiarise data, nor exclude any data that is contrary to your hypothesis. Report all observations made during the research, making sure to avoid selection bias, and identify all possible outliers or results inconsistent to your hypothesis.\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl1\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For original investigations:\ulnone \'a0Present your experimental outcomes in the forms of tables and figures (i.e., images and graphs). Describe these results with a focus on explaining observations, patterns, and trends using scientific theory and reasoning.\cb1 \
\ls7\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For review articles:\ulnone \'a0Describe the results of your review and include any tables or figures that report your results. State the number of articles you found after exclusion; a flow chart is usually helpful in doing this ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://prisma-statement.org/prismastatement/flowdiagram.aspx"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \ul \ulc6 \strokec6 see PRISMA guidelines here}}).\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa225\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 Discussion\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs28 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The discussion section must comprise an interpretation of the results in relation to your original research objective. Use this section to briefly summarize key findings and comment on the significance of these findings, and present possible suggestions for future directions of research.\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl1\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For original investigations:\ulnone \'a0Discuss relevance of your key findings in relation to other literature in the field, presenting other credible sources and academic research to support or contrast your results and interpretations.\cb1 \
\ls8\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For review articles:\ulnone \'a0Briefly discuss the individual articles you found and how their results fit into your review.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa225\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 Conclusion\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs28 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A short paragraph reiterating your primary findings to summarize the main point(s) of the paper.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa225\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 Acknowledgements\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls10\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs28 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Authors may use this section to acknowledge or thank any persons or institutions who helped support the work in any way. This section must disclose any funding for the research completed, including the grant number (if applicable).\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa225\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 References\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs28 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 All information or data from other sources or authors must be appropriately cited at each point in the text where the source is relevant. All sources should be listed in a bibliographic reference section at the end of the paper with the heading \'93References\'94. Bibliographic references should conform to the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlm.nih.gov/bsd/uniform_requirements.html"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \ul \ulc6 \strokec6 Vancouver style}}, in which references are numbered and citations in the text to each reference should be numbers in square brackets, e.g., [1]. If the paper contains any copyright material, such as table, figures, images, or others, the authors must obtain written permission from the copyright holder(s) and provide it to the editor at point of submission.\cb1 \
\ls11\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The use of reference management software such as Mendeley or Zotero are also recommended.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa225\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 Appendices\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs28 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Appendices are optional sections that should include additional tables, figures, or other data beyond what is included in the results sections. An appendix should be able to stand separately from the principal article. Therefore, no references (callouts) to appendix figures or tables should be made in the principal article. If required, the appendix should have its own bibliographic reference list with citations to that list confined to the appendix.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa356\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs42 \cf2 \cb3 Human and Animal Research\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf2 All research carried out using animals must adhere to appropriate ethical principles and have approval from the researcher\'92s institution\'92s animal research or ethics board (if it exists). A signed statement from all authors affirming this, or else proof of institutional approval, will be required for each paper that reports research in which animals were used.\
All research carried out using human subjects must adhere to appropriate ethical principles and have approval from an institution\'92s research ethics board. Proof of institutional approval will be required for each paper that reports research in which human subjects were used.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa356\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs42 \cf2 Article Formatting\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf2 Articles should be submitted in Microsoft Word (.docx) format, as follows:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Double-spaced 12-point Times New Roman font with 2.54 cm margins and all content left-aligned\cb1 \
\ls13\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Guidelines for Figures:\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl1\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Included in the manuscript AND attached as separate image files\cb1 \
\ls13\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Saved as TIFF image format or a vectorized file type (eg. PDF, SVG, EPS)\cb1 \
\ls13\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Between 300-600 dpi\cb1 \
\ls13\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f3 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Any text used within the figure must use Arial or Times New Roman font between 8\'9612-point size\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa140\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Supplementary material, such as videos, are accepted and will be published along with the manuscript in the e-first version of the article on the SFJ website\cb1 \
\ls13\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Bibliographic citations in the reference list and their call-outs in the text should conform to the Vancouver style. For more information on Vancouver style, see\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlm.nih.gov/bsd/uniform_requirements.html"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \ul \ulc6 \strokec6 this page}}. In-text citations to references should be in square brackets; e.g., [1]\cb1 \
\ls13\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Please provide all tables in the text as Word tables - images and tables set up with tabs or spacing are not acceptable. Please also provide tables as images as separate attachments.\'a0 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0 \'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 To ensure your work is formatted correctly, use the following Microsoft Word templates provided by SFJ for both your\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dlR9DNDj33RKmd5pDQ6_RmBT4lER8uhI/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=105197192943580737038&rtpof=true&sd=true"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \ul \ulc6 \strokec6 Title Page\'a0}}and\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.google.com/document/d/12Mkgp-nThZ7JXh40ztnN7vqiz7m3z3A0/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=105197192943580737038&rtpof=true&sd=true"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \ul \ulc6 \strokec6 Manuscript}}. If you are a conference organizer and wish to submit proceedings, follow our\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.google.com/document/d/18tqO0QB4bmhDN2CdM6LqZWLZ7-TLvkOs/edit"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \ul \ulc6 \strokec6 template}}.\
Once your manuscript has met the requirements outlined on this page, please continue onto\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://journal.stemfellowship.org/authors/submitting-a-paper"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \ul \ulc6 \strokec6 Submitting a Paper}}\'a0for instructions on submitting your manuscript and other required documents.\
